WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
You heard a claim once. It sounded strange.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Then you heard it again. Nothing about the evidence changed.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Researchers call the shift in apparent truth the repetition effect.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Even knowing an answer can fail to silence that feeling.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Before buying a promise, ask for the study of this exact product.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Try twelve minutes free. Then decide what a recording is worth to you.
